---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Munex"
	description="Learn about Munex - your trusted source for honest software reviews and comparisons."
	pubDate={new Date('October 01 2026')}
>
	<h2>Hey, I'm Badal 👋</h2>
	<p>
		I started Munex because I was tired of biased software reviews that read like advertisements. 
		Every time I needed to choose a new tool—whether it was a CRM, project management software, 
		or an AI assistant—I found myself wading through content that felt more like sales pitches than honest evaluations.
	</p>

	<p>
		So I decided to build something different.
	</p>

	<h2>What Munex Is About</h2>
	<p>
		Munex is where I share honest, experience-based reviews of the software tools that power modern work. 
		No fluff, no sponsored rankings, no "top 50 tools" lists that nobody actually reads.
	</p>
	<p>
		Every review on this site comes from actual usage. I don't write about tools I haven't tested myself. 
		When I compare ChatGPT to Claude, it's because I've spent months using both for real work. 
		When I review a CRM, it's because I've actually managed contacts and deals in it.
	</p>

	<h2>How I Review Software</h2>
	<p>
		My process is simple but thorough:
	</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Real Usage</strong> — I use each tool for at least 2-4 weeks in actual workflows</li>
		<li><strong>Honest Assessment</strong> — I note what works, what doesn't, and who it's actually for</li>
		<li><strong>Clear Recommendations</strong> — No wishy-washy "it depends" conclusions. I tell you what I'd choose.</li>
		<li><strong>Regular Updates</strong> — Software changes fast. I revisit reviews when tools ship major updates.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>A Note on Affiliate Links</h2>
	<p>
		Some links on Munex are affiliate links. If you sign up for a tool through one of these links, 
		I may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>But here's my promise:</strong> Affiliate relationships never influence my recommendations. 
		I recommend tools because they're good, not because they pay well. 
		I've turned down plenty of sponsorship offers for products I wouldn't genuinely recommend.
	</p>

	<h2>Why Trust Me?</h2>
	<p>
		I'm a software engineer by trade—I've spent years building and working with the kinds of tools I review here. 
		I understand what makes software good (and what makes it frustrating). 
		I care about helping people find tools that actually solve their problems, not just tools that look good in demos.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in Touch</h2>
	<p>
		Have a tool you'd like me to review? Found something wrong in one of my posts? Just want to chat about software?
	</p>
	<p>
		Reach me at <a href="mailto:support@munex.in">support@munex.in</a>. I read every email personally.
	</p>

	<p>
		Thanks for reading. I hope Munex helps you find the right tools for your work.
	</p>
	<p>
		— Badal
	</p>
</Layout>
